keywords:
  - Lean
  - quantum algorithms
  - Hamiltonian simulation
  - differential equations
  - linear systems
abstract: >-
  Formalised sparse-oracle query bounds for Hamiltonian simulation,
  dissipative differential equations and linear-system solving, with
  time-dependent extensions, gate and workspace analyses, and query lower
  bounds. Includes concrete binary-data implementations, selective finite-set
  synthesis and explicit manuscript schedules. Finite-set results assume the
  stated synthesis and source-preparation interfaces. The general,
  non-dissipative constant-coefficient ODE construction is conditional on a
  block-input linear-system solver. The project uses Lean and Mathlib 4.32.1;
  the default build checks 10,055 strict axiom audits. See the README for
  the precise formalisation scope and remaining exclusions.
